 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Clocking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "All eight flip-flops share CP. On its LOW-to-HIGH edge each Qn takes the level on its Dn, provided Dn was steady for the set-up time before the edge and the hold time after it."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Master reset",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Holding MR LOW forces every Q output LOW at once, regardless of CP and the D inputs. After MR goes HIGH again, the recovery time trec must pass before a rising CP edge is counted."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input clamp diodes",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Every input has clamp diodes, so an input can be driven from a voltage above VCC through a series resistor that limits the clamp current."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input levels",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "74HC273 inputs switch at CMOS levels and run from 2.0 V to 6.0 V. 74HCT273 inputs switch at TTL levels and run from 4.5 V to 5.5 V. Both meet JESD7A (2.0 V to 6.0 V) and JESD8C (2.7 V to 3.6 V), with ratings given over both -40 °C to +85 °C and -40 °C to +125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Timing reference levels",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "Timing is measured from input to output at VM: 0.5VCC for the 74HC273, 1.3 V for the 74HCT273, with input pulses of VCC or 3 V and 6 ns edges. Output transition time is taken between 10 % and 90 % of the swing."
  }
 ],
